name: lines scrolled off the top become scrollback, oldest first
source: docs/design/terminal.md, What the VT core handles (scrollback ring)
size: 10x3
input: 1\r\n
input: 2\r\n
input: 3\r\n
input: 4\r\n
input: 5
history: 2
history-row 0: |1|
history-row 1: |2|
row 0: |3|
row 1: |4|
row 2: |5|
---
name: ED 2 clears the screen without moving it to scrollback
source: docs/design/terminal.md, Reconnect and scrollback recovery
size: 10x3
input: a\r\n
input: b\e[2J
history: 0
row 0: ||
row 1: ||
---
name: LF at the bottom margin scrolls only the region's rows
source: DEC VT100 User Guide ch. 3 https://vt100.net/docs/vt100-ug/chapter3.html (DECSTBM, LF/IND)
size: 10x3
input: top\e[2;3r\e[3;1H1\r\n
input: 2\r\n
input: 3
row 0: |top|
row 1: |2|
row 2: |3|
cursor: 1,2
---
name: an autowrapped row keeps its wrapped flag
source: docs/design/terminal.md, What the VT core handles (each row keeps a wrapped flag)
size: 10x3
input: abcdefghijKL
row 0: |abcdefghij|
row 1: |KL|
wrapped 0: true
wrapped 1: false
---
name: filling the last column without wrapping leaves the flag clear
source: docs/design/terminal.md, What the VT core handles (pending wrap)
size: 10x3
input: abcdefghij\r\n
input: x
row 0: |abcdefghij|
row 1: |x|
wrapped 0: false
